# k.values/shards/colours-common: 29 common colour names that CSS does not have (cream, mustard, lemon, amber, apricot, peach, scarlet, ruby ...), each with a usual RGB value (approximate: a name like this has no fixed value).
# sources: hand-core 1 (hand-written in this repository: tools/values-core.mjs)
# license: CC0-1.0
# script: tools/values-core.mjs

@k.values.colour.cream k.values.colour name=cream rgb_about="#FFFDD0" core.source="hand-core 1"
